@SteveSandersonMS when reporting these, one thing that would be super helpful:
1. Save the baseline .dll
2. Open a JS console and put a breakpoint in `aspnetcore-browser-refresh.js` in the `applyBlazorDeltas` function inside the `foreach`.
3. When it hits the breakpoint, in the console display the values of `d.metadataDelta` and `d.ilDelta` and save them. (please make sure that the JS console isn't eliding the middle with "...")
4. hit Continue in the JS debugger and repeat for any other deltas.

The body of the `NavLink` component is a `RenderFragment` lambda, and changing `"Home" => "Home2"` is updating the lambda body.  It's emitting new fields and methods on the lambda, which Mono MBR doesn't support yet.  (ie this is a rude edit - but we need https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/issues/49010 in order to signal it)

(Update, just for my info)
The decompiled relevant part of `NavMenu::BuildRenderTree` body before the update is:
