*Update*
So really this is an issue about supporting updates of lambdas.  Which we should do.  But we're not there yet

(Notes to myself)

Static lambdas generate an interesting closure that tries to only create the delegate for the function just once:
```csharp
public class D {
    public void Foo (Action<D> doer) {
        doer (this);
    }
    public void Bar (int j, int k) {}
}
public class C {
    public int f;
    public void M(D d) {
       int j = 42;
       d.Foo ( (dm1) => dm1.Bar(42,42));
       d.Foo ( (d0) => { HalperClosed(d0); });
       /* ... */
       static void HalperClosed (D d4) { ... }
   }
}
```

generates

```csharp
    [Serializable]
    [CompilerGenerated]
    private sealed class <>c
    {
        public static readonly <>c <>9 = new <>c();

        public static Action<D> <>9__1_0;

        public static Action<D> <>9__1_1;

        internal void <M>b__1_0(D dm1)
        {
            dm1.Bar(42, 42);
        }

        internal void <M>b__1_1(D d0)
        {
            <M>g__HalperClosed|1_4(d0);
        }
    }

    public int f;

    public void M(D d)
    {
        d.Foo(<>c.<>9__1_0 ?? (<>c.<>9__1_0 = new Action<D>(<>c.<>9.<M>b__1_0)));
        d.Foo(<>c.<>9__1_1 ?? (<>c.<>9__1_1 = new Action<D>(<>c.<>9.<M>b__1_1)));
        /* ... */
    }
   /* ... */
}
```

(the lambdas might also be written `static (dm1) => dm1.Bar (42,42)` with `static` explicitly asking for an error if the lambda closes over anything)

An EnC update of the body of a static lambda ends up creating additional static fields in the closure class `<>c` for the new delegates and new static methods for the lambda bodies. (*TODO* double check that it's really the same `<>c` class and not a fresh one!)

So to support these we really need the "add static field" hack from coreclr and "add static method" support.

---

the other interesting cases are for lambdas that capture locals, and lambdas that refer to `this` from the enclosing method (and not to any locals) - the former generate a (nested) display class (possibly including a `this` field if fields are referenced, too).  The latter emit the lambda as an instance method of the class of the enclosing method.  Need to check what the EnC updates do here, but I suspect it's simpler than static lambdas.

also static local functions don't generate these `<>c` delegate caching fields - they end up just doing doing `new Action<X>(MangledLocalFunctionName)` every time through the enclosing function
